+# Factory performance: phase 3
+
+## Scope and reproduction
+
+This phase follows the model/request configuration work documented in
+`model-spec-performance.md` and `request-spec-performance.md`. Existing changes
+from those phases are preserved. Only model and request directories are run,
+separately and sequentially; no system, streaming, or whole-suite invocation.
+No application runtime code is changed.
+
+Both profiling scripts now accept `FACTORY_PROFILE=1`:
+
+```sh
+FACTORY_PROFILE=1 docs/profile-models.sh factories-models-profile-before 12345
+FACTORY_PROFILE=1 docs/profile-requests.sh factories-requests-before 12345
+# After changing factories, repeat with distinct output labels.
+FACTORY_PROFILE=1 docs/profile-models.sh factories-models-after 12345
+FACTORY_PROFILE=1 docs/profile-requests.sh factories-requests-after 12345
+```
+
+Run just one command at a time. On command-time-limited hosts launch a single
+script with `nohup env FACTORY_PROFILE=1 ... > /tmp/factory-run.log 2>&1 &`
+and poll its output. Labels identify artifacts, not code revisions.
+
+`docs/profile_factories.rb` is opt-in instrumentation, not normal spec support.
+It reports calls to Fabrication's definition `fabricate`/`build` methods, elapsed
+monotonic wall time (inclusive and exclusive of nested factory calls), and
+parent-child edges in `tmp/rspec-profile/LABEL.factories.json`. Build calls can
+subsequently be persisted through Rails autosave; these are factory call counts,
+not SQL INSERT counts. Inclusive times overlap and must not be added. Exclusive
+times include model persistence, callbacks, and any non-factory work. A create
+call delegated to build by Fabrication is counted at both definition entry points.
+
+## Findings
+
+The default status factory creates a bookmark in `after_create`. That bookmark
+builds an unrelated account, with a user and signing key, then persists the graph.
+The default user factory creates two login activities in `after_create`, including
+Faker-generated IPs and user agents. Neither collection is required for a valid
+status/user. These are optional history/interactions, not required associations.
+The bookmark/login-activity fabricators already allow specs to request them
+explicitly. The focused groups' bookmark tests already do so.
+
+Removed only these unrelated factory callbacks. Preserved required account
+and user associations, password hashing, key setup, remote status URI setup,
+validations, and all application callbacks. No mutable persisted records are shared
+and no application behavior is stubbed to reduce factory cost.
+
+## Measurements
+
+Same local environment as the earlier phases (Ruby 4.0.6, Rails 8.1.3.1,
+PostgreSQL/Redis, no coverage or parallelization). All runs passed.
+
+| Run | Seed | Examples | RSpec execution | Wall incl. boot |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Models, before (timing only) | 12345 | 1,795 | 57.33 s | 60.63 s |
+| Models, before (factory profiler) | 12345 | 1,795 | 58.08 s | 61.07 s |
+| Requests, before (factory profiler) | 12345 | 1,877 | 99.90 s | 103.47 s |
+| Models, after (factory profiler) | 12345 | 1,801 | 43.74 s | 46.66 s |
+| Requests, after (factory profiler) | 12345 | 1,877 | 86.84 s | 90.09 s |
+| Models, after (setup audit, no profiler) | 67890 | 1,801 | 45.20 s | 48.13 s |
+| Requests, after (setup audit, no profiler) | 67890 | 1,877 | 89.26 s | 92.32 s |
+
+Matched factory-profiled runs: models **24.7% shorter**, requests **13.1%
+shorter**. Combined execution **157.98 -> 130.58 s (17.3% shorter)**; wall
+**164.54 -> 136.75 s (16.9% shorter)**. Six new model regression examples are
+included in the after measurement. Absolute times vary with CI hardware/load.
+
+Relative to the original separately measured phase-1/2 baselines, execution is
+**331.55 -> 130.58 s (2.54x faster)** and wall **337.68 -> 136.75 s (2.47x)**.
+This historical comparison uses different profiling modes; the matched fresh
+before/after comparison above is the evidence for this phase's improvement.
+These are sums of separate runs, not a combined or whole-suite invocation.
+
+### Factory counts and timings
+
+| Factory calls | Models before -> after | Requests before -> after |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| create bookmark | 1,019 -> 18 | 945 -> 9 |
+| create login activity | 270 -> 1 | 2,456 -> 0 |
+| build account | 2,198 -> 1,201 | 3,022 -> 2,086 |
+| build user | 3,001 -> 2,003 | 2,348 -> 1,412 |
+
+Before: `create:status -> create:bookmark` occurred 1,002 times in models,
+936 in requests. After: that edge disappears entirely. Bookmark inclusive
+time dropped **11.65 -> 0.08 s** for models and **10.43 -> 0.14 s** for requests.
+Request login-activity creation cost another **1.80 s** directly. The models'
+remaining login activity is from the explicit-creation regression example.
+Associated users built through an account never ran Fabrication's user
+`after_create` callback, so login-activity counts were not twice *all* user builds.
+
+## Regression coverage
+
+`spec/models/fabricate_spec.rb` adds six examples guarding lean defaults,
+explicit bookmark and login-activity creation, build-only non-persistence,
+required persisted associations, the default password, and remote URI setup.
+Existing examples and assertions are unchanged. Inherited user factories also
+lose the incidental login-history callback; request coverage exercises admin,
+moderator, and private users. Other spec types were not run in this phase.
+
+If a future spec needs interactions or history, create them explicitly with
+`Fabricate(:bookmark, account: ..., status: ...)` or
+`Fabricate(:login_activity, user: ...)`, rather than adding them to the default
+status/user graph. In particular, do not assume a fabricated user has signed in
+just because `current_sign_in_at` is populated.
+
+## Final verification
+
+Both directories passed with seeds 12345 and 67890, run separately. The latter
+used the earlier phases' setup audits (Sidekiq/logger restoration and request
+cache-fixture isolation), without factory instrumentation:
+
+```sh
+VERIFY_SETUP=1 docs/profile-models.sh factories-models-audit 67890
+VERIFY_SETUP=1 docs/profile-requests.sh factories-requests-audit 67890
+bundle exec rspec spec/models --example Fabricate --seed 12345
+```
+
+The six-example filtered run passed after the regression file's final naming/style
+cleanup. RuboCop passed for both changed fabricators, the regression spec, and
+`docs/profile_factories.rb`; shell syntax checks and `git diff --check` passed.
+No existing example needed setup changes to accommodate the leaner factories.
+
+These are shared factory definitions, so other spec types will also stop receiving
+incidental bookmarks/history. Only the requested model/request groups were
+validated; no claim is made about unrun groups. Tests needing those optional
+records should set them up explicitly, as described above.
